      "text": "- Analyzing the Loop\n- I've pinpointed the loop-breaker task's root. It seems malformed JSON within articles, specifically missing quotes in HTML attributes (tag=kimsondreams-21 target=) is causing the system to get stuck. I'm investigating how this corruption occurred and how to prevent it. I'm focusing on the JSON parsing and validation processes.\n- Refining the Approach\n- I'm now zeroing in on a robust solution for the Amazon URL checker and the malformed JSON. The previous attempts to patch files using PYTHONEXEC and SHELL have been unsuccessful. I'm pivoting to a more reliable multi-step SHELL approach, or a verified, robust PYTHONEXEC script, focusing on verifying the changes with grep. My plan is to patch scripts/amazonlinkchecker.cjs with sed to gracefully handle 503 errors and then fix the JSON articles, also using a verified PYTHONEXEC script. I will be verifying both steps with grep.\n- Implementing the Changes",
