      "id": "msg_1772494670463_u1v76",
      "role": "model",
      "text": "- Analyzing System Failures\n- I'm currently observing that task task1772493894762 has entered a \"loop breaker\" state. My primary focus is the poor performance of high-level tools (FILEWRITE, WEBREAD, FILEREPLACE), all showing 0% success. Notably, the SHELL tool is the only one functioning with 68% success rate. I'm formulating a hypothesis based on this.\n- Identifying JSON Corruption\n- I've determined that the failure of high-level tools is probably due to malformed JSON within apple-watch-ultra-2-review.json. A recent cat revealed several missing > characters, indicating the HTML is being improperly parsed. This is leading to \"invalid JSON payload\" errors and explains why writes are failing. I'll focus on fixing the JSON syntax.\n- Validating Configuration Data\n- I'm now focused on validating index.json using Python's json.tool to ensure it's structurally sound. The prior attempts using a cat << 'EOF' approach, while helpful in diagnosing HTML issues in other files, seemed to have produced either single-line JSON or triggered some system sensitivity. There were syntax errors while calling the SHELL command. I'm hoping this validation step is the proper first step. I will attempt to apply fixes to apple-watch-ultra-2-review.json after validation.\n- Refining Error Resolution",
