      "text": "Executing [TOOL] {\n  \"name\": \"PYTHON_EXEC\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"code\": \"import json\\nimport os\\n\\npath = 'data/articles/apple-watch-ultra-2-review.json'\\ncontent = {\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"apple-watch-ultra-2-review\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Apple Watch Ultra 2 Review: The Ultimate Rugged Smartwatch\\\",\\n    \\\"subtitle\\\": \\\"Comprehensive review of Apple's most advanced outdoor smartwatch for adventurers and athletes\\\",\\n    \\\"author\\\": \\\"Technova Team\\\",\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2025-01-15\\\",\\n    \\\"category\\\": \\\"REVIEWS\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"Tech\\\", \\\"Apple\\\", \\\"Wearables\\\", \\\"Smartwatch\\\", \\\"Fitness\\\", \\\"Accessories\\\"],\\n    \\\"image\\\": \\\"images/articles/apple-watch-ultra-2-main.jpg\\\",\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p>The Apple Watch Ultra 2 represents the pinnacle of wearable technology for adventurers and athletes. Building upon the original Ultra success, this second-generation model brings refinements in performance, display brightness, and sustainability.</p><h2>Design and Build Quality</h2><p>The Ultra 2 maintains the distinctive 49mm titanium case. The aerospace-grade titanium is both lightweight and incredibly durable, capable of withstanding extreme conditions from deep-sea diving to mountain climbing.</p><h2>Display: Brighter Than Ever</h2><p>The Always-On Retina display now reaches 3000 nits of peak brightness, making it easily readable even in direct sunlight. The sapphire crystal front provides exceptional scratch resistance.</p><h2>Performance and Battery Life</h2><p>Powered by the S9 SiP chip, the Ultra 2 delivers smooth performance for all tasks. Battery life extends up to 36 hours in normal use and up to 72 hours in Low Power Mode.</p><h2>Where to Buy</h2><div class='product-recommendation'><h3>Check Price on Amazon</h3><p><a href='https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CHX3TW6T?tag=kimsondreams-21' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Buy Apple Watch Ultra 2 on Amazon</a></p></div>\\\"\\n}\\n\\nwith open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\\n    json.dump(content, f, indent=2)\\n\\nindex_path = 'data/articles/index.json'\\nwith open(index_path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\\n    index_data = json.load(f)\\n\\nprint(f\\\"SUCCESS: Fixed {path}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"SUCCESS: Validated {index_path} (contains {len(index_data)} entries)\\\")\"\n  }\n}",
