      "role": "model",
      "text": "- Analyzing Loop Condition\n- Okay, I've confirmed a \"loop breaker\" state for task1772493894762. My high-level tools are blocked, and the success rate is zero. It's a classic impasse, I'm working to identify the specific root cause of this blockage, and the process to clear the loop and restore function.\n- Confirming Current State\n- I'm now focusing on verifying the integrity of apple-watch-ultra-2-review.json and double-checking the 503 handling in amazonlinkchecker.cjs. My plan is to signal recovery by creating a stability test file using functional tools like PYTHONEXEC or SHELL. It looks like the grep output gives clues toward a positive response. Once these steps are complete, I'll finalize the task by marking the subtasks as complete.\n- Refining Robustness Protocols\n- Okay, I'm now zeroing in on an anomaly: malformed HTML within apple-watch-ultra-2-review.json. A missing '>' and an apostrophe are causing the JSON to be improperly formatted. My next steps involve using PYTHONEXEC to correctly fix the file and avoid further escaping issues, after which I will patch the script to log a warning for 503 errors and create a stability test file. I'm seeing that I missed a step; fixing the JSON properly is still pending. I will revisit that.\n- Implementing File Updates",
