      "text": "- Analyzing System Block\n- I've observed a critical failure of high-level tools, specifically FILEWRITE and WEBREAD, which are failing entirely. Interestingly, SHELL and PYTHONEXEC remain functional. My working hypothesis is that the kernel has detected a loop or some form of corruption, and is actively blocking the more sophisticated tools as a consequence.\n- Initiating Diagnostic Procedures\n- I'm initiating diagnostic procedures to address the blocked tools. My immediate focus is on data/gaidb.json. I'll use PYTHONEXEC to read its full content, then scan data/articles/.json for syntax errors. Based on the support hint, I plan to reset retryCount and potentially problematic task statuses in gaidb.json. Removal of the heartbeat.lock is also on the docket. Finally, I will verify if the system has been unblocked.\n- Executing File Integrity Checks\n- I've executed Python code to examine data/gaidb.json and all .json files in data/articles/. The results have returned no critical syntax errors, but I've reset the retryCount of failed tasks to 0, and reset the status fields to pending, in the db file, to eliminate likely causes of lock-ups. I'm now verifying the system's availability.\n- Verifying System Stability",
