      "role": "model",
      "text": "- Analyzing Blocked Tools\n- I've observed a \"loop breaker\" state where core tools like FILEWRITE, WEBREAD, and TASKACTION are consistently failing. My hypothesis is that the kernel is actively blocking them based on either success rates in data/gaidb.json or detection of repetitive behavior in the data/repetitive directory. I'm focusing on the criteria used for blockage, and I need to establish if it is by specific success rates or some other form of loop detection.\n- Verifying Kernel Reset\n- I'm now focused on confirming the success of the repair script. Reading package.json with FILEREAD was recently successful, so that seems like a good sign. However, the TOOLSTATS still report 0% for blocked tools. I hypothesize that a \"tick\" from a successful high-level operation might be required to refresh the kernel's internal state, or the gaidb.json may still hold outdated information. I'm moving to the high-level tool tests to advance progress.",
