      "text": "- Analyzing Tool Access\n- I've observed a critical constraint; high-level tools are failing, yet shell and Python execution remain operational. I suspect the kernel is selectively blocking specific tools based on the current state. My focus is now on discerning the precise criteria for this tool access restriction.\n- Investigating Kernel Block\n- I'm now zeroing in on a possible in-memory trigger for the tool block. Recent attempts to reconstruct data/gaidb.json and clear lock files haven't worked; the kernel persists with 0% success. I'll read the watchdog log for clues. Afterward, I'll test file access via FILEREAD to see if the block persists before attempting a TASKACTION update. The goal is loop resolution and restored tools.\n- Exploring Script Availability\n- The kernel hasn't updated its internal state, despite a PYTHONEXEC claiming completion. I've noted a hint to use fixloopbreaker.py. I'll first check if that script exists. Then, I'll examine the watchdog log and loop configuration to understand what might be blocking task updates. The goal is to break the loop and understand task completion issues.\n- Expressing Gratitude and Hope",
