\": \"system\",\n      \"text\": \"STAGE: Model: deepseek-v3.2:cloud (Role: architecture)\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772496058709,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772496058744_jnvkl\",\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"text\": \"STAGE: Support hint requested for active task: Autonomia: Samorozwój (loop_breaker)\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772496058744,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772496069494_13uj1\",\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"text\": \"STAGE: Support idea: SUPPORT_HINT: Use `SHELL` with `sed -i '' 's/\\\\\\\"retryCount\\\\\\\": [0-9]*/\\\\\\\"retryCount\\\\\\\": 0/g' data/gai_db.json` to reset counts without parsing JSON, then `rm -f data/heartbeat.lock`.\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772496069494,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772496069509_bmo9w\",\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"text\": \"STAGE: Ollama: oczekiwanie na odpowiedź\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772496069509,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772496075534_ugajr\",\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"text\": \"STAGE: Ollama: odpowiedź odebrana (6s)\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772496075534,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772496075553_l64zl\",\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"text\": \"STAGE: Analiza odpowiedzi\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772496075553,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772496075568_sxhb2\",\n      \"role\": \"model\",\n      \"text\": \"- Analyzing System Block\\n- I've noted the system is in a \\\"loop breaker\\\" state, and high-level tools are failing miserably. SHELL and PYTHONEXEC are still operational but are a bit wonky. I'm hypothesizing that the kernel is blocking the