 \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772497274679_edfm7\",\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"text\": \"STAGE: Analiza odpowiedzi\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772497274679,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772497274698_8xhme\",\n      \"role\": \"model\",\n      \"text\": \"- Analyzing System Constraints\\n- I've observed a critical system state: \\\"loop breaker\\\" is active. High-level tools like FILEWRITE, WEBREAD, and TASKACTION are completely blocked, while SHELL and PYTHONEXEC remain functional. SHELL's success rate sits at 68%. My current hypothesis is that a kernel-level mechanism is intentionally inhibiting these high-level actions based on success rates. The next step is to further probe the kernel for confirmation.\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772497274698,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"thought\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772497274706_nvp9f\",\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"text\": \"STAGE: Analiza odpowiedzi...\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772497274706,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772497274730_wlu3b\",\n      \"role\": \"model\",\n      \"text\": \"AUTONOMY BLOCKED: TOOL success rate 0%. Choose alternative.\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772497274730,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772497274744_ls4hc\",\n      \"role\": \"model\",\n      \"text\": \"AUTONOMY BLOCKED: TOOL success rate 0%. Choose alternative.\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772497274744,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772497274759_8kzmw\",\n      \"role\": \"model\",\n      \"text\": \"AUTONOMY BLOCKED: TOOL success rate 0%. Choose alternative.\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772497274759,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772