 and WEBREAD, with zero success. My hypothesis is that the kernel is enforcing these blocks based on the data in data/gaidb.json. I'm starting to build a model that connects these observations.\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772498372646,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"thought\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772498372653_rx9wf\",\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"text\": \"STAGE: Analiza odpowiedzi...\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772498372653,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772498372674_dvsn6\",\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"text\": \"STAGE: Wykonywanie: [TOOL] {\\\"name\\\": \\\"SHELL\\\", \\\"arguments\\\": {\\\"command\\\": \\\"ls -la...\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772498372674,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772498372688_vtsui\",\n      \"role\": \"model\",\n      \"text\": \"Executing [TOOL] {\\\"name\\\": \\\"SHELL\\\", \\\"arguments\\\": {\\\"command\\\": \\\"ls -la .gaios/ && tail -n 50 .gaios/watchdog.log\\\"}}\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772498372688,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"exec\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772498372695_9mp9c\",\n      \"role\": \"model\",\n      \"text\": \"AUTONOMY BLOCKED: TOOL success rate 0%. Choose alternative.\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772498372695,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772498372709_9qzht\",\n      \"role\": \"model\",\n      \"text\": \"AUTONOMY BLOCKED: TOOL success rate 0%. Choose alternative.\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772498372709,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"msg_1772498373752_uwl8h\",\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"text\": \"[SYSTEM/INFO] Autonomy Tick\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772498373752,\n      \"isAutonomous\": true,\n      \"logType\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id