PYTHONEXEC and SHELL were unsuccessful in fully lifting the block. It looks like the kernel is either caching the state or the execution did not fully reset the block in the kernel's perception. I'm considering the possibility of kernel state caching, which means the previous execution didn't fully resolve the kernel's perception of the blocked state. The support hint is now the focus.\",\n      \"role\": \"architecture\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek-v3.2:cloud\",\n      \"source\": \"autonomy\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"handoff_1772499032066\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1772499032066,\n      \"summary\": \"- Analyzing Aggressive Loop\\n- I've observed an \\\"Aggressive Loop Detected\\\" state. High-level tools like FILEWRITE, WEBREAD, and TASKACTION are completely blocked, but SHELL and PYTHONEXEC are still functional. My current hypothesis is that a specific file or state within data/ is triggering the kernel's loop protection.\\n- Investigating Persistent Loop\\n- I've confirmed gaidb.json is empty, yet the \\\"Aggressive Loop Detected\\\" persists. The kernel likely caches state data, or another file is involved. I'm now leveraging SHELL to examine the watchdog log, specifically using tail -n 50 .gaios/watchdog.log to pinpoint the trigger, as the support hint suggested.\",\n      \"role\": \"architecture\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek-v3.2:cloud\",\n      \"source\": \"autonomy\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blogs\": [],\n  \"memories\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mem_1771493339757_4xvdlz5\",\n      \"type\": \"conversation\",\n      \"content\": \"Hej\",\n      \"metadata\": {\n        \"timestamp\": 1771493339757,\n        \"userId\": \"User\",\n        \"importance\": 0.8,\n        \"tags\": [\n          \"user_input\",\n          \"terminal\"\n        ],\n        \"context\": \"Terminal conversation\",\n        \"emotionalTone\": \"neutral\",\n        \"relatedMemories\": [\n          \"mem_1771493331391_jxltcei\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"accessStats\": {\n        \"accessCount\": 0,\n        \"lastAccessed\": 1771493339757,\n        \"firstCreated\": 1771493339757,\n        \"relevanceScore\": 1\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"pinned_articles_guide\",\n      \"title\": \"HOW_TO_WRITE_ARTICLES\",\n      \"type\": \"pinned\",\n      \"content\": \"# Przewodnik GAI: Tworzenie i Edytowanie Artykułów na Blogu Technologicznym\\n\\n## UWAGA KRYTYCZNA ⚠️\\nTen przewodnik powstał po gruntownym audycie bazy artykułów, podczas którego wykryto liczne błędy związane z nieaktualnymi datami, modelami produktów i wydarzeniami technologicznymi. **KAŻDY ARTYKUŁ MUSI BYĆ WERYFIKOWANY POD KĄTEM AKTUALNOŚCI PRZED PUBLIKACJĄ.**\\n\\n## 1. ZASADY PODSTAWOWE\\n\\n### 1. Aktualność Informacji - PRIORYTET #1\\n- **NIGDY nie używaj przyszłych dat** (np. 2026, 2027)\\n- **ZAWSZE sprawdzaj aktualne modele produktów** przed napisaniem artykułu\\n- **WERYFIKUJ daty premier produktów** w oficjalnych źródłach\\n- **AKTUALIZUJ informacje o wydarzeniach technologicznych** (CES, Prime Day, itp.)\\n\\n## 2. STRUKTURA PLIKU ARTYKUŁU JSON\\n\\n### 2.1 Wymagane Pola\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"unikalny-identyfikator-artykulu\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Tytuł Artykułu\\\",\\n  \\\"subtitle\\\": \\\"Podtytuł opisujący treść\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": \\\"Imię Nazwisko\\\",\\n  \\\"date\\\": \\\"YYYY-MM-DD\\\",\\n  \\\"category\\\": \\\"REVIEWS|COMPARISONS|NEWS|PROMOTIONS\\\",\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"tag1\\\", \\\"tag2\\\", \\\"tag3\\\"],\\n  \\\"image\\\": \\\"images/articles/nazwa-obrazu.jpg\\\",\\n  \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p>Treść artykułu w HTML...</p>\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 2.2 Sprawdzanie Spójności\\n- **ID musi odpowiadać tytułowi i treści**\\n- **Tytuł musi odpowiadać treści artykułu**\\n- **Data musi być realistyczna** (nie przyszła)\\n- **Tagi muszą odpowiadać treści**\\n\\n## 3. PROCES TWORZENIA ARTYKUŁU KROK PO KROKU\\n\\n### KROK 1: Badanie i Weryfikacja\\n1. **Sprawdź aktualne informacje o produkcie w internecie**\\n   - Oficjalne strony producentów\\n   - Aktualne specyfikacje techniczne\\n   - Daty premier i dostępności\\n   - produkt powinien się znajdowac w ofercie amazon\\n   \\n2. **Weryfikuj modele produktów**\\n   - Apple: sprawdź najnowsze modele na apple.com\\n   - Samsung: sprawdź aktualną linię Galaxy\\n   - Inne marki: sprawdź oficjalne strony\\n\\n3. **Sprawdź daty wydarzeń**\\n   - CES: zawsze styczeń\\n   - Prime Day: zwykle lipiec\\n   - Black Friday: listopad\\n   - Back to School: sierpień-wrzesień\\n   - Inne wydarzenia\\n\\n### KROK 2: Planowanie Treści\\n1. **Określ typ artykułu**\\n   - REVIEWS: recenzje produktów\\n   - COMPARISONS: porównania produktów\\n   - NEWS: aktualności technologiczne\\n   - PROMOTIONS: promocje i oferty\\n   - ANNOUNCEMENTS: zapowiedzi produktów\\n   - PRODUCT RUMORS - plotki co jest tworzone w największych firmach\\n   - inne typy\\n\\n2. **Zaplanuj strukturę**\\n   - Wprowadzenie\\n   - Sekcje tematyczne (Design, Performance, itp.)\\n   - Zdjęcia i opisy\\n   - Podsumowanie/Werdykt\\n   - Linki affiliate\\n   - TYLKO JĘZYK ANGIELSKI\\n\\n### KROK 3: Tworzenie ID i Metadanych\\n1. **Utwórz unikalny ID**\\n   ```\\n   Format: nazwa-produktu-typ-artykulu\\n   Przykład: iphone-16-pro-max-review\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **Ustaw datę**\\n   ```\\n   ZAWSZE: Sprawdzaj aktualną datę w internecie\\n   Format: \\\"YYYY-MM-DD\\\"\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Wybierz odpowiednie tagi**\\n   - Nazwa marki (Apple, Samsung, Sony)\\n   - Typ produktu (iPhone, MacBook, Headphones)\\n   - Kategoria (Review, Comparison)\\n\\n### KROK 4: Pisanie Treści\\n1. **Struktura HTML**\\n   ```html\\n   <p>Paragraf wprowadzający</p>\\n   \\n   <h2>Nagłówek Sekcji</h2>\\n   <p>Treść sekcji</p>\\n   \\n   <div class=\\\"article-image-wrapper\\\">\\n       <img src=\\\"images/articles/nazwa.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"Opis\\\" class=\\\"article-image\\\">\\n       <p class=\\\"image-caption\\\">Podpis obrazu</p>\\n   </div>\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **Linki Amazon (WAŻNE!)**\\n   ```html\\n   <a href=\\\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/PRODUCT_ID?tag=kimsondreams-21\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">Tekst linku</a>\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Sekcja rekomendacji produktów**\\n   ```html\\n   <div class=\\\"product-recommendation\\\">\\n       <h3>Where to Buy</h3>\\n       <p>Opis z linkami Amazon</p>\\n   </div>\\n   ```\\n\\n### KROK 5: Dobór Obrazów\\n1. **Nazewnictwo plików**\\n   ```\\n   Format: nazwa-produktu-typ.jpg\\n   Przykład: iphone-16-pro-max-main.jpg\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **Lokalizacja**\\n   ```\\n   Ścieżka: images/articles/nazwa-pliku.jpg\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Wymagania techniczne**\\n   - Format: JPG lub PNG\\n   - Rozdzielczość: minimum 800px szerokości\\n   - Rozmiar: maksymalnie 500KB\\n\\n## 4. LISTA KONTROLNA PRZED PUBLIKACJĄ\\n\\n### ✅ Weryfikacja Treści\\n- [ ] Data artykułu aktualna z internetu\\n- [ ] Wszystkie modele produktów są aktualne\\n- [ ] Wydarzenia technologiczne mają poprawne daty\\n- [ ] Tytuł odpowiada treści artykułu\\n- [ ] ID artykułu jest unikalny i opisowy\\n\\n### ✅ Weryfikacja Techniczna\\n- [ ] Plik JSON ma poprawną składnię\\n- [ ] Wszystkie wymagane pola są wypełnione\\n- [ ] **KRYTYCZNE**: Każdy link Amazon został przetestowany ręcznie\\n- [ ] **KRYTYCZNE**: Wszystkie linki prowadzą do właściwych produktów\\n- [ ] **KRYTYCZNE**: Brak duplikatów linków dla różnych produktów\\n- [ ] Linki Amazon zawierają tag affiliate (?tag=kimsondreams-21)\\n- [ ] Produkty na Amazon są dostępne (nie \\\"Currently unavailable\\\")\\n- [ ] Obrazy istnieją w folderze images/articles/\\n- [ ] HTML jest poprawnie sformatowany\\n\\n### ✅ Weryfikacja SEO\\n- [ ] Tytuł zawiera główne słowo kluczowe\\n- [ ] Tagi są relevantne do treści\\n- [ ] Alt text dla obrazów jest opisowy\\n- [ ] Linki zewnętrzne mają target=\\\"_blank\\\"\\n\\n## 5. NAJCZĘSTSZE BŁĘDY DO UNIKANIA\\n\\n### ❌ BŁĘDY KRYTYCZNE\\n1. **Przyszłe daty** (2026, 2027) - NIGDY JAKO DATA ARTYKUŁU!\\n2. **Nieaktualne modele Apple** (sprawdzaj najnowsze modele) - SPRAWDZAJ!\\n3. **Niepoprawne daty wydarzeń** (sprawdzaj oficjalne daty) - WERYFIKUJ!\\n4. **Niespójność tytuł-treść** - KONTROLUJ!\\n\\n### ❌ Błędy Techniczne\\n1. Niepoprawny JSON (brakujące przecinki, cudzysłowy)\\n2. Nieistniejące ścieżki do obrazów\\n3. Brakujące tagi affiliate w linkach Amazon\\n4. Niepoprawne formatowanie HTML\\n\\n### ❌ Błędy Merytoryczne\\n1. Nieaktualne specyfikacje produktów\\n2. Błędne ceny i dostępność\\n3. Nieweryfikowane informacje techniczne\\n4. Brakujące źródła dla twierdzeń\\n\\n## 6. NARZĘDZIA WERYFIKACJI\\n\\n### 6.1 Sprawdzanie Aktualności\\n- **Apple**: apple.com - oficjalne specyfikacje\\n- **Samsung**: samsung.com - aktualne modele\\n- **Amazon**: amazon.com - ceny i dostępność\\n- **Tech News**: techcrunch.com, theverge.com\\n\\n### 6.2 Walidacja JSON\\n- Użyj walidatora JSON online\\n- Sprawdź składnię przed zapisem\\n- Testuj w przeglądarce\\n\\n### 6.3 Sprawdzanie Linków Amazon - PROCEDURA OBOWIĄZKOWA\\n\\n#### 🔍 AUDYT LINKÓW PRZED PUBLIKACJĄ\\n**KAŻDY link Amazon MUSI być sprawdzony przed publikacją artykułu!**\\n\\n1. **Weryfikacja Dostępności Produktu**\\n   - Kliknij każdy link Amazon w artykule\\n   - Sprawdź czy prowadzi do właściwego produktu\\n   - Upewnij się, że produkt jest dostępny (nie \\\"Currently unavailable\\\")\\n   - Sprawdź czy cena jest aktualna\\n\\n2. **Kontrola Poprawności Linków**\\n   ```\\n   ✅ POPRAWNY FORMAT:\\n   https://www.amazon.com/dp/PRODUCT_ID?tag=kimsondreams-21\\n   \\n   ❌ BŁĘDNE FORMATY:\\n   - Linki bez tagu affiliate\\n   - Linki do konkretnych wariantów (kolor, rozmiar)\\n   - Linki do nieistniejących produktów\\n   - Linki prowadzące do złych produktów\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Sprawdzanie Spójności Produkt-Link**\\n   - **KRYTYCZNE**: Link do iPhone 16 Pro Max NIE MOŻE prowadzić do iPhone 15\\n   - **KRYTYCZNE**: Link do Sony WH-1000XM5 NIE MOŻE prowadzić do Bose\\n   - **KRYTYCZNE**: Link do ASUS ROG NIE MOŻE prowadzić do Dell\\n\\n4. **Procedura Naprawy Błędnych Linków**\\n   ```\\n   Jeśli link jest błędny:\\n   1. Znajdź właściwy produkt na Amazon\\n   2. Skopiuj ASIN (kod produktu)\\n   3. Utwórz nowy link: https://www.amazon.com/dp/ASIN?tag=kimsondreams-21\\n   4. Zamień błędny link na poprawny\\n   5. Przetestuj nowy link\\n   ```\\n\\n5. **Alternatywne Rozwiązanie - Linki Wyszukiwania**\\n   ```\\n   Jeśli konkretny produkt nie jest dostępny:\\n   https://www.amazon.com/s?k=nazwa+produktu&tag=kimsondreams-21\\n   \\n   Przykłady:\\n   - https://www.amazon.com/s?k=iphone+16+pro+max&tag=kimsondreams-21\\n   - https://www.amazon.com/s?k=sony+wh-1000xm5&tag=kimsondreams-21\\n   - https://www.amazon.com/s?k=asus+rog+zephyrus+g14&tag=kimsondreams-21\\n   ```\\n\\n#### 🚨 NAJCZĘSTSZE BŁĘDY LINKÓW (WYKRYTE W AUDYCIE)\\n\\n1. **Ten sam link dla różnych produktów**\\n   - ❌ Trzy różne laptopy z tym samym linkiem Amazon\\n   - ✅ Każdy produkt ma unikalny, właściwy link\\n\\n2. **Link prowadzi do złego produktu**\\n   - ❌ Link \\\"Sony WH-1000XM5\\\" prowadzi do Bose QuietComfort\\n   - ✅ Link prowadzi dokładnie do opisywanego produktu\\n\\n3. **Nieaktualne linki produktów**\\n   - ❌ Link do iPhone 15 w artykule o iPhone 16\\n   - ✅ Link odpowiada modelowi opisywanemu w artykule\\n\\n4. **Brakujące tagi affiliate**\\n   - ❌ https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0C6J8JQ6K\\n   - ✅ https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0C6J8JQ6K?tag=kimsondreams-21\\n\\n#### 📋 LISTA KONTROLNA LINKÓW AMAZON\\n\\n**Przed publikacją artykułu sprawdź:**\\n- [ ] Każdy link Amazon został przetestowany\\n- [ ] Wszystkie linki prowadzą do właściwych produktów\\n- [ ] Produkty są dostępne na Amazon\\n- [ ] Wszystkie linki zawierają tag affiliate\\n- [ ] Nie ma duplikatów linków dla różnych produktów\\n- [ ] Ceny produktów są aktualne\\n- [ ] Linki nie prowadzą do błędnych wariantów produktu\\n\\n#### 🔧 NARZĘDZIA DO SPRAWDZANIA LINKÓW\\n\\n1. **Ręczne testowanie**\\n   - Otwórz każdy link w nowej karcie\\n   - Sprawdź czy to właściwy produkt\\n   - Zweryfikuj dostępność\\n\\n2. **Sprawdzanie ASIN**\\n   ```\\n   ASIN to unikalny kod produktu Amazon\\n   Format: B0XXXXXXXXX (10 znaków)\\n   Znajdziesz go w URL produktu\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Weryfikacja tagów affiliate**\\n   ```\\n   Każdy link MUSI zawierać: ?tag=kimsondreams-21\\n   Sprawdź na końcu każdego URL\\n   ```\\n\\n#### ⚠️ PROCEDURA AWARYJNA DLA BŁĘDNYCH LINKÓW\\n\\n**Jeśli wykryjesz błędny link w opublikowanym artykule:**\\n\\n1. **NATYCHMIAST** oznacz artykuł do poprawy\\n2. Znajdź wszystkie błędne linki w artykule\\n3. Wyszukaj właściwe produkty na Amazon\\n4. Zamień błędne linki na poprawne\\n5. Przetestuj wszystkie nowe linki\\n6. Zapisz poprawiony artykuł\\n7. Przeprowadź pełny audyt pozostałych linków w artykule\\n\\n**PAMIĘTAJ**: Błędne linki Amazon to utrata potencjalnych prowizji i zaufania czytelników!\\n\\n## 7. PRZYKŁAD POPRAWNEGO ARTYKUŁU\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"iphone-16-pro-max-review\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"iPhone 16 Pro Max Review: Apple's Latest Flagship Smartphone\\\",\\n  \\\"subtitle\\\": \\\"A comprehensive review of Apple's most advanced iPhone yet\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": \\\"John Smith\\\",\\n  \\\"date\\\": \\\"2025-01-15\\\",\\n  \\\"category\\\": \\\"REVIEWS\\\",\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"Apple\\\", \\\"iPhone 16 Pro Max\\\", \\\"Smartphone\\\", \\\"Review\\\"],\\n  \\\"image\\\": \\\"images/articles/iphone-16-pro-max-main.jpg\\\",\\n  \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p>Apple's iPhone 16 Pro Max represents the pinnacle of smartphone technology in 2025...</p>\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 8. PROCEDURA AWARYJNA\\n\\nJeśli wykryjesz błąd w opublikowanym artykule:\\n\\n1. **NATYCHMIAST zatrzymaj publikację**\\n2. **Zidentyfikuj typ błędu** (data, model, treść)\\n3. **Popraw błąd** zgodnie z tym przewodnikiem\\n4. **Przeprowadź pełną weryfikację** artykułu\\n5. **Przetestuj poprawki** przed ponowną publikacją\\n\\n## 9. SPECJALNE INSTRUKCJE DLA RÓŻNYCH TYPÓW ARTYKUŁÓW\\n\\n### 9.1 Recenzje Produktów (REVIEWS)\\n- **Zawsze sprawdź najnowszą wersję produktu**\\n- **Weryfikuj specyfikacje techniczne**\\n- **Sprawdź aktualną cenę na Amazon**\\n- **Dodaj sekcję \\\"Where to Buy\\\" z linkami affiliate**\\n\\n### 9.2 Porównania (COMPARISONS)\\n- **Upewnij się, że porównujesz aktualne modele**\\n- **Sprawdź daty premier wszystkich produktów**\\n- **Weryfikuj dostępność na rynku**\\n- **Dodaj tabelę porównawczą**\\n\\n### 9.3 Aktualności (NEWS)\\n- **Sprawdź datę wydarzenia/ogłoszenia**\\n- **Weryfikuj informacje w oficjalnych źródłach**\\n- **Nie używaj przyszłych dat**\\n- **Dodaj źródła informacji**\\n\\n### 9.4 Promocje (PROMOTIONS)\\n- **Sprawdź aktualność promocji**\\n- **Weryfikuj daty trwania ofert**\\n- **Testuj linki do produktów**\\n- **Dodaj informację o ograniczeniach czasowych**\\n\\n## 10. WORKFLOW KONTROLI JAKOŚCI\\n\\n### Przed Rozpoczęciem Pisania:\\n1. Sprawdź aktualne informacje o produkcie\\n2. Weryfikuj modele i specyfikacje\\n3. Sprawdź konkurencyjne artykuły\\n4. Zaplanuj strukturę artykułu\\n\\n### Podczas Pisania:\\n1. Używaj aktualnych dat i informacji\\n2. Sprawdzaj każdy fakt przed dodaniem\\n3. Weryfikuj linki Amazon\\n4. Dodawaj odpowiednie obrazy\\n\\n### Po Napisaniu:\\n1. Sprawdź składnię JSON\\n2. Weryfikuj wszystkie linki\\n3. Testuj wyświetlanie artykułu\\n4. Przeprowadź końcową kontrolę faktów\\n\\n## PODSUMOWANIE\\n\\n**PAMIĘTAJ**: Każdy artykuł to reprezentacja marki. Błędy w datach, modelach produktów czy wydarzeniach technologicznych podważają wiarygodność całego bloga. **ZAWSZE weryfikuj informacje przed publikacją!**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SPECYFIKACJA TECHNICZNA PLIKU JSON (ARTYKUŁ)\\n\\n- Plik: umieść w `articles/`, nazwa w formacie `slug.json` (np. `iphone-16-pro-max-review.json`).\\n- Kodowanie: UTF‑8. Zawartość w pełni poprawny JSON.\\n- Pola wymagane:\\n  - `id`: unikalny identyfikator (slug), np. `iphone-16-pro-max-review`.\\n  - `title`: tytuł artykułu.\\n  - `author`: autor (np. `Technova Team`).\\n  - `date`: data publikacji w formacie `YYYY-MM-DD`.\\n  - `category`: typ artykułu. Dozwolone wartości: `NEWS`, `REVIEWS`, `COMPARISONS`, `PROMOTIONS`, `ANNOUNCEMENTS`.\\n  - `content`: treść HTML (sekcje, akapity, linki). Bez skryptów.\\n- Pola opcjonalne, zalecane:\\n  - `subtitle`: krótki opis.\\n  - `image`: URL głównego obrazu (lokalnie używaj `images/articles/...`).\\n  - `tags`: lista tematów, służy do filtrowania w menu tematycznym. Rekomendowane tematy: `Tech`, `AI`, `Gaming`, `Audio`, `Productivity`, `Dev`, `Smart Home`, `Accessories`, `Hardware`, `Science`.\\n  - `gallery`: lista obiektów `{ src, alt, caption }` dla dodatkowych zdjęć.\\n  - `affiliateLinks`: lista obiektów `{ label, url }` z poprawnym tagiem Amazon.\\n\\n### Minimalny przykład\\n\\n```\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"iphone-16-pro-max-review\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"iPhone 16 Pro Max Review\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": \\\"Technova Team\\\",\\n  \\\"date\\\": \\\"2024-11-02\\\",\\n  \\\"category\\\": \\\"REVIEWS\\\",\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"Tech\\\", \\\"Apple\\\", \\\"Smartphone\\\"],\\n  \\\"image\\\": \\\"images/articles/iphone-16-pro-max.jpg\\\",\\n  \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p>Full long-form review content...</p>\\\",\\n  \\\"gallery\\\": [\\n    { \\\"src\\\": \\\"images/articles/iphone-16-pro-max-1.jpg\\\", \\\"alt\\\": \\\"Back panel\\\", \\\"caption\\\": \\\"Matte finish\\\" }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Zasady walidacji\\n\\n- `category` wpływa na pierwszy rząd filtrów (NEWS/REVIEWS/PROMOTIONS/itd.).\\n- `tags` wpływają na drugi rząd filtrów (tematy). Aby artykuł był widoczny po kliknięciu `TECH`, dodaj w `tags` co najmniej jeden z synonimów: `Tech`, `Technology`, `Gadgets`, `Devices`. Analogicznie dla `AI`, `Gaming`, `Audio`, `Productivity`, `Dev`, `Smart Home`, `Accessories`, `Hardware`, `Science`.\\n- Obrazy lokalne trzymaj w `images/articles/`. Używaj rozsądnych rozmiarów i proporcji.\\n- Treść `content` musi być bogata, z pełnymi akapitami, bez skrótów i bez skryptów.\\n\\n### Kluczowe Zasady:\\n1. **Aktualność przede wszystkim** - żadnych przyszłych dat\\n2. **Weryfikacja faktów** - sprawdzaj każdą informację\\n3. **Spójność treści** - tytuł musi odpowiadać zawartości\\n4. **Poprawność techniczna** - testuj JSON i linki\\n5. **SEO i UX** - dbaj o jakość treści dla użytkowników\\n\\n---\\n\\n*Ten przewodnik został zaktualizowany w styczniu 2025. Przestrzeganie tych wytycznych jest OBOWIĄZKOWE.*\\n\",\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"path\": \"/Users/jakubnetza/Desktop/GAI/HOW_TO_WRITE_ARTICLES.MD\",\n        \"sha256\": \"2b11b44923130607d8ebfe147c1fb333b8b5d20f9d50008493c47731b4c36df5\"\n      },\n      \"updatedAt\": 1771494323521,\n      \"createdAt\": 1771494323521\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"pinned_system_paths\",\n      \"title\": \"SYSTEM_PATHS\",\n      \"type\": \"pinned\",\n      \"content\": \"{\\n  \\\"dataDir\\\": \\\"/Users/jakubnetza/Desktop/GAI/data\\\",\\n  \\\"fsRoot\\\": \\\"/Users/jakubnetza/Desktop/GAI/data/fs\\\",\\n  \\\"articlesDir\\\": \\\"/Users/jakubnetza/Desktop/GAI/data/articles\\\",\\n  \\\"articlesIndex\\\": \\\"/Users/jakubnetza/Desktop/GAI/data/articles/index.json\\\",\\n  \\\"ftp\\\": {\\n    \\\"rootPath\\\": \\\"/public_html/kimsondreams/\\\",\\n    \\\"remoteArticlesDir\\\": \\\"\\\"\\n  }\\n}\",\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"dataDir\": \"/Users/jakubnetza/Desktop/GAI/data\",\n        \"fsRoot\": \"/Users/jakubnetza/Desktop/GAI/data/fs\",\n        \"articlesDir\": \"/Users/jakubnetza/Desktop/GAI/data/articles\"\n      },\n      \"updatedAt\": 1771494323521,\n      \"createdAt\": 1771494323521\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"realtime_sources_cache\",\n      \"title\": \"REALTIME_SOURCES\",\n      \"type\": \"web\",\n      \"content\": \"URL: https://hnrss.org/frontpage\\nSTATUS: 200\\nCONTENT:\\nHacker News: Front Page https://news.ycombinator.com/ Hacker News RSS https://hnrss.org/ hnrss v2.1.1 Mon, 02 Mar 2026 23:36:53 +0000 Article URL: https://www.rac.ca/rac-responds-to-the-closure-of-the-weatherradio-service-in-canada/ Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47225505 Points: 12 # Comments: 3 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 23:03:59 +0000 https://www.rac.ca/rac-responds-to-the-closure-of-the-weatherradio-service-in-canada/ da768 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47225505 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47225505 Article URL: https://andrewvanner.github.io/som/SoM_CC_Process_Day.pdf Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47225318 Points: 21 # Comments: 0 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 22:49:47 +0000 https://andrewvanner.github.io/som/SoM_CC_Process_Day.pdf haunter https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47225318 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47225318 Article URL: https://www.svd.se/a/K8nrV4/metas-ai-smart-glasses-and-data-privacy-concerns-workers-say-we-see-everything Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47225130 Points: 221 # Comments: 121 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 22:32:35 +0000 https://www.svd.se/a/K8nrV4/metas-ai-smart-glasses-and-data-privacy-concerns-workers-say-we-see-everything sandbach https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47225130 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47225130 Article URL: https://blog.sturdystatistics.com/posts/type_hint/ Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47224832 Points: 17 # Comments: 1 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 22:04:56 +0000 https://blog.sturdystatistics.com/posts/type_hint/ kianN https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47224832 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47224832 I built a voice agent from scratch that averages ~400ms end-to-end latency (phone stop → first syllable). That’s with full STT → LLM → TTS in the loop, clean barge-ins, and no precomputed responses. What moved the needle: Voice is a turn-taking problem, not a transcription problem. VAD alone fails; you need semantic end-of-turn detection. The system reduces to one loop: speaking vs listening. The two transitions - cancel instantly on barge-in, respond instantly on end-of-turn - define the experience. STT → LLM → TTS must stream. Sequential pipelines are dead on arrival for natural conversation. TTFT dominates everything. In voice, the first token is the critical path. Groq’s ~80ms TTFT was the single biggest win. Geography matters more than prompts. Colocate everything or you lose before you start. GitHub Repo: https://github.com/NickTikhonov/shuo Follow whatever I next tinker with: https://x.com/nick_tikhonov Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47224295 Points: 67 # Comments: 22 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 21:23:40 +0000 https://www.ntik.me/posts/voice-agent nicktikhonov https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47224295 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47224295 Article URL: https://take.surf/2026/03/01/welcome-back-to-macintosh Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47224118 Points: 168 # Comments: 102 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 21:09:47 +0000 https://take.surf/2026/03/01/welcome-back-to-macintosh Udo_Schmitz https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47224118 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47224118 A little weekend project, made so I can pause/play/rewind directly on the piano, when learning a song by ear. Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47223863 Points: 29 # Comments: 10 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 20:50:03 +0000 https://github.com/vustagc/pianoterm vustagc https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47223863 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47223863 Article URL: https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/british-columbia/b-c-adopting-year-round-daylight-time-9.7111657 Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47223620 Points: 297 # Comments: 171 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 20:30:52 +0000 https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/british-columbia/b-c-adopting-year-round-daylight-time-9.7111657 ireflect https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47223620 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47223620 A filter list for uBO that blurs all video and non-follower content from Instagram. Works on mobile with uBO Lite. related: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47016443 Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47223147 Points: 87 # Comments: 21 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 19:50:32 +0000 https://gist.github.com/shraiwi/009c652da6ce8c99a6e1e0c86fe66886 shraiwi https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47223147 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47223147 Article URL: https://starlightconvenience.net/#that-shape-had-none Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47222226 Points: 69 # Comments: 13 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 18:45:12 +0000 https://starlightconvenience.net/#that-shape-had-none casmalia https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47222226 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47222226 Govbase tracks every bill, executive order, and federal regulation from official sources (Congress.gov, Federal Register, White House). An AI pipeline breaks each one down into plain-language summaries and shows who it impacts by demographic group. It also ties each policy directly to bias-rated news coverage and politician social posts on X, Bluesky, and Truth Social. You can follow a single bill from the official text to how media frames it to what your representatives are saying about it. Free on web, iOS, and Android. https://govbase.com I'd love feedback from the community, especially on the data pipeline or what policy areas/features you feel are missing. Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47220809 Points: 135 # Comments: 62 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 17:08:53 +0000 https://govbase.com foxfoxx https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47220809 https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47220809 Article URL: https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/reflex/jobs Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47220666 Points: 0 # Comments: 0 ]]> Mon, 02 Mar 2026 17:01:20 +0000 https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/reflex/jobs apetuskey https://news.ycombinator.com/i\\n\\n---\\n\\nURL: https://techcrunch.com/feed/\\nSTATUS: 200\\nCONTENT:\\nTechCrunch https://techcrunch.com/ Startup and Technology News Mon, 02 Mar 2026 23:51:04 +0000 en-US hourly 1 https://wordpress.org/?v=6.9.1 https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/02/cropped-cropped-favicon-gradient.png?w=32 TechCrunch https://techcrunch.com/ 32 32 Stripe wants to turn your AI costs into a profit center https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/stripe-wants-to-turn-your-ai-costs-into-a-profit-center/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 23:18:27 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098620 Geopolitical drama reportedly stalls IPO of SoftBank-backed PayPay https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/geopolitical-drama-reportedly-stalls-ipo-of-softbank-backed-paypay/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 23:01:57 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098631 No one has a good plan for how AI companies should work with the government https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/openai-anthropic-department-of-defense-war-hegseth-ai-companies-work-with-us-government/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 22:59:10 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098660 A new app alerts you if someone nearby is wearing smart glasses https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/nearby-glasses-new-app-alerts-you-wearing-smart-glasses-surveillance-meta-snap-bluetooth/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 22:40:00 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098085 Instagram tracked growing usage while targeting teens, lawyers argue https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/instagram-tracked-growing-usage-while-targeting-teens-lawyers-argue/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 22:23:48 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098594 Users are ditching ChatGPT for Claude — here’s how to make the switch https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/users-are-ditching-chatgpt-for-claude-heres-how-to-make-the-switch/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 18:42:11 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098443 Paramount+ and HBO Max to merge into one streaming service after WBD deal closes https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/paramount-and-hbo-max-to-merge-into-one-streaming-service-after-wbd-deal-closes/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 18:34:19 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098525 Tech workers urge DOD, Congress to withdraw Anthropic label as a supply-chain risk https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/tech-workers-urge-dod-congress-to-withdraw-anthropic-label-as-a-supply-chain-risk/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 17:18:34 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098455 X adds &#8216;Paid Partnership&#8217; labels so creators can ditch the hashtags https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/x-ads-paid-partnership-labels-for-creators-so-they-can-ditch-the-hashtags/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 16:25:08 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098425 Hacktivists claim to have hacked Homeland Security to release ICE contract data https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/hacktivists-claim-to-have-hacked-homeland-security-to-release-ice-contract-data/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 16:11:56 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098421 A married founder duo&#8217;s company, 14.ai, is replacing customer support teams at startups https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/a-married-founder-duos-company-14-ai-is-replacing-customer-support-teams-at-startups/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 15:14:36 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3096045 Apple speeds up the iPad Air with an M4 upgrade, starting at $599 https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/apple-speeds-up-the-ipad-air-with-an-m4-upgrade-starting-at-599/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 15:06:20 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098385 Apple bakes in AI smarts into its new $599 iPhone 17e https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/apples-bakes-in-ai-smarts-into-its-new-599-iphone-17e/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 14:53:14 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098386 Hackers and internet outages hit Iran amid US air strikes https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/hackers-and-internet-outages-hit-iran-amid-u-s-air-strikes/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 14:16:53 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098364 MyFitnessPal has acquired Cal AI, the viral calorie app built by teens https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/myfitnesspal-has-acquired-cal-ai-the-viral-calorie-app-built-by-teens/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 14:00:00 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098039 Parade&#8217;s Cami Tellez announces new creator economy marketing platform, $4M in funding https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/parades-cami-tellez-announces-new-creator-economy-marketing-platform-4m-in-funding/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 14:00:00 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098324 Anthropic&#8217;s Claude reports widespread outage https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/anthropics-claude-reports-widespread-outage/ Mon, 02 Mar 2026 13:31:49 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098361 Polymarket saw $529M traded on bets tied to bombing of Iran https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/01/polymarket-saw-529m-traded-on-bets-tied-to-bombing-of-iran/ Sun, 01 Mar 2026 19:05:35 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098336 Let’s explore the best alternatives to Discord https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/01/best-discord-alternatives-age-verification-identity-privacy/ Sun, 01 Mar 2026 19:00:01 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3096153 Google looks to tackle longstanding RCS spam in India — but not alone https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/01/google-looks-to-tackle-longstanding-rcs-spam-in-india-but-not-alone/ Sun, 01 Mar 2026 17:30:00 +0000 https://techcrunch.com/?p=3098313\\n\\n---\\n\\nURL: https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\\nSTATUS: 200\\nCONTENT:\\nThe Verge The Verge is about technology and how it makes us feel. Founded in 2011, we offer our audience everything from breaking news to reviews to award-winning features and investigations, on our site, in video, and in podcasts. 2026-03-02T22:29:46+00:00 https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/verge-rss-large_80b47e.png?w=150&amp;h=150&amp;crop=1 Stevie Bonifield https://www.theverge.com/?p=887885 2026-03-02T17:29:46-05:00 2026-03-02T17:29:46-05:00 Anthropic is making it easier to switch to its Claude AI from other chatbots with an update that brings Claude's memory feature to users on the free plan, along with a new prompt and dedicated tool for importing data from other chatbots. These upgrades could allow users who have been using rivals like OpenAI's ChatGPT or Google's Gemini to quickly copy the data their preferred AI has collected on them and bring it over to Anthropic's chatbot. That way, they don't have to \\\"start over\\\" teaching Claude the context and history their previous chatbot already knows. The option to import and export memories from Claude has been available since O … Read the full story at The Verge. ]]> Sheena Vasani https://www.theverge.com/?p=887839 2026-03-02T17:03:09-05:00 2026-03-02T17:03:09-05:00 The AirPods 4 are the best entry-level AirPods yet. | Photo by Chris Welch / The Verge It’s a good day for Apple fans on a budget. Not only did the company introduce a new budget phone , its entry-level AirPods 4 are also on sale. Right now, you can snag a pair of Apple’s AirPods 4 starting at just $89 ($30 off) at Walmart . The model with active noise-cancellation are also down to their second best price to date, going for $119 ($60 off) at Amazon and Walmart . AirPods 4 Where to Buy: $129 $89 at Walmart $179 $119 at Amazon (with ANC) $179 $119 at Walmart (with ANC) The AirPods 4 are the best and most comfortable entry-level earbuds from Apple yet. They deliver fuller bass along with clearer, more detailed sound than previous models, and even now match the AirPods Pro in terms of voice call quality. They also boast an upgraded IP54 rating for water and dust resistance, meaning they can withstand light rain and sweaty workouts. As with other Apple headphones, they also play nicely with Apple devices, offering conveniences like automatic switching, access to hands-free Siri, and Apple TV support. If you’re willing to spend $30 extra, the ANC model offers all the same features while also doing a surprisingly good job of tuning out the world. They can’t rival the AirPods Pro , but they still dramatically cut down on ambient and low-frequency noise on planes and in offices, particularly with music playing. The ANC earbuds also offer a transparency mode that sounds natural, along with support for tracking via Apple’s Find My App, a wireless charging case, and live translation through an iOS 26 update . ]]> Sheena Vasani https://www.theverge.com/?p=887570 2026-03-02T16:50:57-05:00 2026-03-02T15:41:50-05:00 Unlike its predecessor, the iPhone 17E supports MagSafe. | Image: Apple The iPhone 17 lineup now has a “budget” option. Announced this week , the iPhone 17E will hit stores on Wednesday, March 11th, starting at $599, with preorders opening on March 4th. The 6.1-inch phone joins the rest of Apple’s iPhone 17 lineup, which includes the iPhone 17 ($799), the more powerful iPhone 17 Pro ($1,099), and the iPhone 17 Pro Max ($1,199), as well as the ultra-thin iPhone Air ($999). Unlike last year’s iPhone 16E , the 17E features MagSafe and Qi2 wireless charging, along with the faster A19 chip found in the iPhone 17 and twice as much base storage (256GB vs. 128GB). It also features a sharper, more durable display, retains support for Apple Intelligence, and includes a 48-megapixel “fusion” camera that enables 2x telephoto shots, all of which bring it closer to Apple’s more premium phones. But at $599, the 17E doesn’t include all of the bells and whistles found in the rest of Apple’s current iPhone lineup. For example, it only has a 6.1-inch 60Hz display&nbsp;— the smallest display of any iPhone 17 series phone — and lacks features like an always-on display and Dynamic Island, a pill-shaped cutout that shows info, like ride-share updates, at a glance. It’s also noticeably dimmer, with a peak brightness of 1,200 nits. Camera hardware is another differentiator. While the 17E, Air, and standard iPhone 17 all share a 48-megapixel main sensor, the iPhone 17 has a dedicated ultrawide camera, which also enables macro photography for close-up shots. The 17 and Air also offer an 18-megapixel front-facing camera — the 17E only has a 12-megapixel shooter — which could translate to sharper selfies and clearer video calls. The Pro and Pro Max models expand further with more advanced camera arrays, including the addition of dedicated telephoto cameras. Plus, all except the 17E include the Camera Control button, which is designed to help people quickly launch the camera and adjust various settings. Unsurprisingly, charging speeds and battery life also differ. The 17E supports MagSafe charging with Qi2 support, allowing for wireless charging at up to 15W, while the iPhone 17, iPhone Air, and both Pro models support faster 25W wireless charging. Apple says the 17E can charge up to 50 percent in 30 minutes, compared to about 20 minutes for the higher-end models. Battery life increases as you move up the lineup, with the 17E rated for up to 26 hours of video playback, while the iPhone Air and the larger Pro Max models last longer (up to 39 hours, in some instances). Those are just some of the main highlights, though. If you want to get into the nitty-gritty, we’ve compiled all the specs together below, letting you see how each phone stacks up to the others. Category iPhone 17E iPhone Air iPhone 17 iPhone 17 Pro iPhone 17 Pro Max Operating system iOS 26 iOS 26 iOS 26 iOS 26 iOS 26 Apple Intelligence support Yes Yes Yes Yes Yes Display 6.1\\n\\n---\\n\\nURL: https://www.engadget.com/rss.xml\\nSTATUS: 200\\nCONTENT:\\nhttps://www.engadget.com/ en-US copyright Yahoo 2026 Mon, 02 Mar 2026 22:17:14 +0000 Yahoo http://yahoo.com Australia&#39;s government may take a strict stance on ensuring younger users cannot access AI chatbots. Reuters reports that Australian regulators may require app storefronts to block AI services that do not implement age verification for restricting mature content by March 9.&nbsp; &quot;eSafety will use the full range of our powers where there is non-compliance,&quot; a representative for the commissioner said in a statement to the publication. Those paths could include &quot;action in respect of gatekeeper services such as search engines and app stores that provide key points of access to particular ‌services.&quot; A review by Reuters found that of 50 leading text-based AI chat services in the region, only nine had introduced or shared plans for age assurance. Eleven services reportedly &quot;had blanket content filters or planned to block all Australians from using their service,&quot; according to the report, leaving a large number that had not taken public action a week ahead of the country&#39;s deadline. Failure to comply could see AI companies face fines of up to A$49.5 million ($35 million). The question of which parties are responsible for keeping children from accessing potentially harmful content is being debated around the world. In the US, for instance, Apple and Google have been lobbying to have the task delegated to platforms rather than app store operators. The language from the Australian regulators about all stores is hardly definitive at this stage, but given the breadth of its sweeping ban on the use of social media and some highly social digital platforms for citizens under age 16 enacted last year, an aggressive stance seems to align with leaders&#39; priorities.&nbsp; This article originally appeared on Engadget at https://www.engadget.com/ai/australia-will-consider-requiring-app-stores-to-block-ai-services-without-age-verification-221714252.html?src=rss]]> engadget_479 f1087080-c45c-4761-8887-54726f0608b1 Mon, 02 Mar 2026 22:17:14 +0000 1772489846 2026-03-02T22:17:29+00:00 headline Anthropic is bringing another paid feature to Claude&#39;s free tier. The next time you chat with Claude, you&#39;ll have the option to have it reference your previous conversation to inform its outputs. Anthropic first made its chatbot capable of remembering past interactions last August , before giving it the ability to compartmentalize memories in the fall . Making memory a free feature is well-timed; earlier today Anthropic made it easier for users to import their past conversations with a competing chatbot to Claude.&nbsp;If after enabling memory you decide to turn it off, you can either pause the feature, preserving Claude’s memories for use down the road, or completely delete them so they’re not saved on Anthropic’s servers. Claude is enjoying new-found popularity, having recently jumped to the number one spot in the App Store&#39;s free app charts. This comes while Anthropic is engaged in a high-stakes contract dispute with the US government over AI safeguards. On Friday, US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth labeled the company a &quot;supply chain risk&quot; after it refused to sign a contract that would allow the Pentagon to use Anthropic models for mass surveillance against Americans and in fully autonomous weapons. Following Hegseth&#39;s announcement, Anthropic vowed to challenge the designation. As of right now, we’re waiting to see how things play out, and what it might mean for Anthropic. This article originally appeared on Engadget at https://www.engadget.com/ai/anthropic-brings-memory-to-claudes-free-plan-220729070.html?src=rss]]> engadget_479 2a2056f7-0108-4756-8fdd-dc580a9f8d75 Mon, 02 Mar 2026 22:07:29 +0000 1772489255 2026-03-02T22:07:37+00:00 headline Call of Duty is getting a new battle royale mode later this month. The popular first-person shooter will introduce Black Ops Royale as a free game mode on March 13.&nbsp; Black Ops Royale pays homage to Blackout, the series&#39; first foray into a battle royale game mode back in CoD: Black Ops 4 . Matches will have 100 players dropping in as four-person teams. The mode takes place on the massive Avalon map, but there will be no familiar Warzone features like loadouts, the gulag, or buy stations. Instead, it&#39;s all about the scavenging the weapons from the recent Black Ops 7 game and upgrading them.&nbsp; According to the team&#39;s announcement, there will be other familiar features from the Blackout days such as the weapon handling and bullet drop that have been reimagined for modern-day Warzone players. You&#39;ll also be able to further customize your play style with an open-ended perks system, another nod to the original Call of Duty BR perk mechanic. This article originally appeared on Engadget at https://www.engadget.com/gaming/call-of-duty-will-add-black-ops-royale-a-new-free-game-mode-coming-march-13-211733205.html?src=rss]]> engadget_479 cefa0124-838b-4de9-86a5-d3a0021144a5 Mon, 02 Mar 2026 21:17:33 +0000 1772486258 2026-03-02T21:17:40+00:00 headline Starlink is getting ready to launch its second generation of satellites, and it&#39;s expected to match the speeds of a traditional terrestrial network. During a keynote at Mobile World Congress, Starlink execs detailed the roadmap for the company&#39;s upgrade towards the next generation of satellites called V2. &quot;The goal of Starlink Mobile ... is to provide a terrestrial-like connectivity when you&#39;re connected to the satellite system,&quot; Michael Nicolls, SpaceX&#39;s senior vice president of Starlink engineering, said during the MWC keynote. &quot;In the right conditions, it should look and feel like you&#39;re connected to a high-performing 5G terrestrial network.&quot; Nicolls detailed that the V2 satellite constellation could offer download speeds up to 150 Mbps in ideal conditions, comparing it to a broadband experience. According to \\n\\n---\\n\\nURL: https://arstechnica.com/rss/\\nSTATUS: 200\\nCONTENT:\\nArs Technica https://arstechnica.com Serving the Technologist since 1998. News, reviews, and analysis. Mon, 02 Mar 2026 22:39:12 +0000 en-US hourly 1 https://cdn.arstechnica.net/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/cropped-ars-logo-512_480-60x60.png Ars Technica https://arstechnica.com 32 32 Clueless cops post seized crypto wallet password. $5M quickly stolen. https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2026/03/oops-south-korean-cops-lost-5m-in-seized-crypto-after-leaking-wallet-password/ https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2026/03/oops-south-korean-cops-lost-5m-in-seized-crypto-after-leaking-wallet-password/#comments Mon, 02 Mar 2026 22:27:52 +0000 https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2026/03/oops-south-korean-cops-lost-5m-in-seized-crypto-after-leaking-wallet-password/ Soon after South Korean police posted a press release boasting about seizing $5.6 million worth of cryptocurrency from 124 wealthy tax evaders, cops realized that they had mistakenly posted images that made it possible for a thief to quickly steal most of the seized assets. Eventually, the press release was removed, but not before it was grabbed by local media outlets and tech publications covering the theft. Bleeping Computer shared a screenshot of the retracted images, which showed a handwritten note next to a Ledger device that's used as a so-called \\\"cold wallet\\\" to store crypto out of reach of online threats. Clearly legible in the photo, the note contained a complete mnemonic recovery phrase that anyone can use as a master key to move assets off the cold wallet to a new wallet without any additional PIN or permissions required. Read full article Comments ]]> 20 Ivan Sherstiuk | iStock / Getty Images Plus Charter gets FCC permission to buy Cox and become largest ISP in the US https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2026/03/fcc-lets-charter-buy-cox-says-no-reason-to-worry-about-higher-internet-prices/ https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2026/03/fcc-lets-charter-buy-cox-says-no-reason-to-worry-about-higher-internet-prices/#comments Mon, 02 Mar 2026 18:19:03 +0000 https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2026/03/fcc-lets-charter-buy-cox-says-no-reason-to-worry-about-higher-internet-prices/ Charter Communications, operator of the Spectrum cable brand, has obtained Federal Communications Commission permission to buy Cox and surpass Comcast as the country's largest home Internet service provider. Charter has 29.7 million residential and business Internet customers compared to Comcast's 31.26 million . Buying Cox will give Charter another 5.9 million Internet customers . The FCC approved the deal on Friday, but the companies still need Justice Department approval and sign-offs from states including California and New York. Opponents of Charter's $34.5 billion acquisition told the FCC that eliminating Cox as an independent entity will make it easier for Charter and Comcast to raise prices. But the FCC dismissed those concerns on the grounds that Charter and Cox don't compete directly against each other in the vast majority of their territories. Read full article Comments ]]> 102 Getty Images | Kevin Dietsch A Cox service van is parked at a Cox Communications warehouse on May 16, 2025 in Springfield, Virginia. Iowa county adopts strict zoning rules for data centers, but residents still worry https://arstechnica.com/ai/2026/03/iowa-county-adopts-strict-zoning-rules-for-data-centers-but-residents-still-worry/ https://arstechnica.com/ai/2026/03/iowa-county-adopts-strict-zoning-rules-for-data-centers-but-residents-still-worry/#comments Mon, 02 Mar 2026 15:34:42 +0000 https://arstechnica.com/ai/2026/03/iowa-county-adopts-strict-zoning-rules-for-data-centers-but-residents-still-worry/ PALO, Iowa—There are two restaurants in Palo, not counting the chicken wings and pizza sold at the only gas station in town. All three establishments, including the gas station, stand on the same half-mile stretch of First Street, an artery that divides the marshy floodplain of the Cedar River to the east from hundreds of acres of cornfields on the west. During historic flooding in 2008, the Cedar River surged 10 feet above its previous record, cresting at 31 feet and wiping out homes and businesses well outside the floodplain. Read full article Comments ]]> 81 QTS A rendering of the QTS data center currently under construction in Cedar Rapids, Iowa. $599 M4 iPad Air is a lot like the old one, but with a substantial RAM boost https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/03/apple-keeps-the-ipad-air-fresh-with-m4-chip-upgrade-and-12gb-of-ram/ https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/03/apple-keeps-the-ipad-air-fresh-with-m4-chip-upgrade-and-12gb-of-ram/#comments Mon, 02 Mar 2026 15:06:00 +0000 https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/03/apple-keeps-the-ipad-air-fresh-with-m4-chip-upgrade-and-12gb-of-ram/ As expected, Apple has announced a mild update for the iPad family's middle child today. The new iPad Air is a lot like the old one, but it replaces the Apple M3 chip with an M4. That M4 also comes with a less-expected upgrade: a jump from 8GB of RAM to 12GB, which should be helpful for those using iPadOS 26's multi-window multitasking features. The iPad Air still comes in 11-inch and 13-inch versions that start at $599 and $799, respectively; the only disappointment is that these entry-level models still come with 128GB of storage. A 256GB storage upgrade will run you $100, and 512GB (+$300) and 1TB (+$500) versions are also available. Preorders go live on March 4, and the tablet will be available on March 11. The M4 iPad Air uses the same design as the M2 version from 2024 and the M3 version from last year. The M2 version of the Air was a gently tweaked version of the M1 iPad Air, but it was different enough not to be compatible with all the same accessories; most notably, the M2-and-later Airs use the Apple Pencil Pro accessory and aren’t compatible with the second-generation Pencil. Read full article Comments ]]> 54 Apple Apple's M4 iPad Air. Research roundup: Six cool science stories we almo\\n\\n---\\n\\nURL: https://www.wired.com/feed/rss\\nSTATUS: 200\\nCONTENT:\\nWIRED The latest from www.wired.com https://www.wired.com © Condé Nast 2026 en-US Mon, 02 Mar 2026 23:48:44 +0000 Missile Attacks Are Overwhelming the Gulf. Delivery Drivers Are Still on the Roads https://www.wired.com/story/with-missile-attacks-overhead-in-the-gulf-delivery-drivers-are-still-on-the-road/ 69a5cdf63ea3f0e5be7c34ff Mon, 02 Mar 2026 21:34:36 +0000 Missile and drone attacks have disrupted daily life, but delivery drivers are still diligently navigating streets to drop off orders across the region. Business Business / Startups Uber, logistics, Middle East, Iran, gig economy, delivery Carla Sertin Condé Nast Special Order Iranian Ayatollah Khamenei’s Death Sparks Revolt Among Kalshi Customers https://www.wired.com/story/iranian-ayatollah-khameneis-death-sparks-revolt-among-kalshi-customers/ 69a59c9453b95f8fe738644d Mon, 02 Mar 2026 20:08:38 +0000 How Kalshi decided to settle a market tied to Iran’s supreme leader prompted anger among traders who felt the rules weren’t clear. Business Business / Startups prediction markets, Iran, Kalshi, Polymarket, war, Middle East Kate Knibbs Condé Nast Crisis Mode Attacks on GPS Spike Amid US and Israeli War on Iran https://www.wired.com/story/gps-attacks-on-ships-spike-amid-the-us-and-israeli-war-on-iran/ 69a5a29afb8b2b3db6442fa2 Mon, 02 Mar 2026 18:34:25 +0000 New analysis shows that attacks on satellite navigation systems have impacted some 1,100 ships in the Middle East since the US and Israel attacked Iran on February 28. Security Security / Cyberattacks and Hacks Security / National Security Security / Security News Iran, Middle East, war, navigation, GPS, shipping, Israel, Military, supply chain, oil Matt Burgess Condé Nast Blast Radius Our Favorite Budget TV Is on Sale https://www.wired.com/story/vizio-tv-deal-226/ 69a5cb93a94ced1863932f80 Mon, 02 Mar 2026 18:25:57 +0000 This 55-inch Vizio isn’t the fanciest, but you could do a lot worse for under $300. Gear Gear / Deals Gear / Products Gear / Products / Televisions TVs, Television, Shopping, Deals Brad Bourque Condé Nast Deal of the Day War in Iran Spiked Oil Prices. Trump Will Decide How High They Go https://www.wired.com/story/war-in-iran-sent-oil-prices-up-trump-will-decide-how-high-they-go/ 69a57dc199ba745596a012d0 Mon, 02 Mar 2026 16:03:36 +0000 The conflict in the Middle East is driving oil prices up in a midterm year when Americans are already focused on high energy bills. Science Science / Environment Politics / Policy Security / National Security Security / Security News Iran, Donald Trump, National Affairs, oil, Energy, war, Military Molly Taft Condé Nast High times Apple Gives the iPad Air a Small Power Boost https://www.wired.com/story/apple-ipad-air-m4-2026/ 699f83e966b5135e06cef480 Mon, 02 Mar 2026 14:36:31 +0000 The iPad Air enjoys a relatively modest update with the M4 chip and 12 gigabytes of RAM. Gear Gear / Produ